        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: yǐnliào",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "yǐnliào — \"drink; soft drink\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nǐ xiǎng hē shénme yǐnliào — What would you like to drink?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "yǐnliào is built from yǐn 'to drink' and liào, both inherited from Middle Chinese, 'imX and lew (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). The dictionary glosses the second 'to measure' and lists it with a departing tone too, lewH, the one liào continues; how the pair came to mean a drink is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for asking for what I want."
            }
